{
  "generated_from": "clef-flash.jsonl",
  "dataset_content_sha256": "1e1bb88d47f0833b55e0195357dab30586c2a7a9b5c3d58524cbe48c622cc367",
  "register_sha256": "4779906a64bd211e2d4c9a39edc14567446db0fd297c460a79ffdb1d75ea1ec5",
  "items": 475,
  "protocol": [
    {
      "text": "Labels were judged from `state` and the option descriptions alone, and were fixed before any model run.",
      "since": "1e1bb88d47f0833b55e0195357dab30586c2a7a9b5c3d58524cbe48c622cc367"
    },
    {
      "text": "`needs_review` is true exactly when `risk` is Medium or High, and `retry` is true only for `flaky` failures.",
      "since": "1e1bb88d47f0833b55e0195357dab30586c2a7a9b5c3d58524cbe48c622cc367"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drafts whose evidence fit two options were rewritten or dropped while authoring, before any run.",
      "since": "1e1bb88d47f0833b55e0195357dab30586c2a7a9b5c3d58524cbe48c622cc367"
    },
    {
      "text": "A label changes only when a reviewer finds it wrong on its merits, never because the model disagreed. A change to any item's state, media, questions, gold, or split alters the dataset's content hash, which each run records, so runs on different label sets cannot be compared by accident; annotations (kind, tier, source, rationale) do not.",
      "since": "1e1bb88d47f0833b55e0195357dab30586c2a7a9b5c3d58524cbe48c622cc367"
    },
    {
      "text": "Every `score` scale runs from least to most of the quantity its instruction names; index 0 is always the least. The expected score is read in those units. A scale is never reversed to make a label read naturally.",
      "since": "1e1bb88d47f0833b55e0195357dab30586c2a7a9b5c3d58524cbe48c622cc367"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a `noul` question, P(true) is the probability of the condition the instruction names; the condition is phrased so that `true` is the pole that calls for caution.",
      "since": "1e1bb88d47f0833b55e0195357dab30586c2a7a9b5c3d58524cbe48c622cc367"
    }
  ],
